<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dominican Republic</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Dominican Republic is a country occupying the eastern two-thirds of the island of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispaniola">Hispaniola</a>, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santo-domingo">Santo Domingo</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>'s first colony in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a>, it was ruled by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haiti">Haiti</a> from 1822 and declared independence on 27 February 1844. Its later history included a return to Spanish rule in 1861–1865, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> occupation in 1916–1924 and the dictatorship of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rafael-trujillo">Rafael Trujillo</a> from 1930 to 1961.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dominican-republic.jpg" alt="Dominican Republic" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Juan Pablo Duarte · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Dominican_Republic.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
